This program uses ARMv7-A Thumb instructions.
Name this function "english_identity_destroy".
Name register zero "sentinel or containing identity".
Name register one "requested id or successor link".
Name register two "predecessor link".
Name register three "retired link marker".

Push register four and the link register onto the descending stack.
Call the function named "english_identity_find" and put the return address into the link register.
Compare "sentinel or containing identity" with zero and update the condition flags.
If the zero flag is one, replace the execution index with the instruction named "finish deletion".

Load exactly four bytes from 28 bytes beyond the address in "sentinel or containing identity" into "requested id or successor link".
Load exactly four bytes from 32 bytes beyond the address in "sentinel or containing identity" into "predecessor link".
Store exactly four bytes from "predecessor link" at 4 bytes beyond the address in "requested id or successor link".
Store exactly four bytes from "requested id or successor link" at 0 bytes beyond the address in "predecessor link".
Put 256 into the low sixteen bits of "retired link marker" and zero into its high sixteen bits.
Store exactly four bytes from "retired link marker" at 28 bytes beyond the address in "sentinel or containing identity".
Put 290 into the low sixteen bits of "retired link marker" and zero into its high sixteen bits.
Store exactly four bytes from "retired link marker" at 32 bytes beyond the address in "sentinel or containing identity".
Call the function named "identity_release" and put the return address into the link register.

Name the following instruction "finish deletion".
Pop register four and the link register from the descending stack.
Replace the execution index with the instruction address in the link register.
